WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.374 --> 00:00:02.748
[LASER SHOTS]

00:00:02.748 --> 00:00:03.870
 Come on, Wolverine.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:04.920
Let's go.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.780
 Eat dirt, Cyclops.

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:08.460
X-Men don't cut and run.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:13.770
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:15.040
 What's up, everyone.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:18.060
This is "Disney+ Deets,"
where we break down everything

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.320
you need to know
about your favorite

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.190
Disney+ movies and series.

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:21.990
I'm Kenneth.

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:22.957
MARCELLUS: And I'm Marcellus.

00:00:22.957 --> 00:00:24.900
And not to toot our own
horns, but we're pretty

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.760
much the biggest
Disney+ fans out there.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:28.860
 No, let's do it.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:31.440
Toot toot, beep beep,
that's right.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:32.310
 Let's get into it.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:40.910
KENNETH: 12-year-old Kenneth
is (SINGSONG) excited.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:43.250
Today's video is about
one of our favorite

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:47.660
super hero shows of all time,
"X-Men: The Animated Series."

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:50.780
Let's take it all the way
back to 1963 when Marvel

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:54.470
all-stars Jack Kirby and Stan
Lee created the first "X-Men"

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:55.330
comic book.

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:57.740
Originally, the
characters were teenagers

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:00.470
in identical blue uniforms
and their dialogue

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.330
was all quips and wisecracks.

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:06.020
In 1975, Marvel decided
to reimagine the X-Men

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:07.380
as a more international team.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:08.180
MARCELLUS: Yes.

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:09.200
And you know what, Ken?

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.400
Diversity is key.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.440
Writer Len Wein and
artist Dave Cockrum

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:13.880
came up with, among others--

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:16.550
Wolverine, who's Canadian,
and our favorite mistress

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.890
of the elements from
Northern Africa, Storm.

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:21.200
KENNETH: But this wasn't
just a new team roster.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.720
It set a whole new
tone for the series.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:26.603
The heroes were adults with
real relatable problems.

00:01:26.603 --> 00:01:27.770
MARCELLUS: And I
just love how they

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:28.713
interacted with each other.

00:01:28.713 --> 00:01:30.080
I wanted to like, sit
and chill with them

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:31.370
and just talk about stuff--
KENNETH: Right.

00:01:31.370 --> 00:01:32.300
MARCELLUS: --that was going on.
KENNETH: Right.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.350
MARCELLUS: What was
the next mission?

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:34.160
KENNETH: Exactly.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.110
President of Fox
Kids Margaret Loesch

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:38.810
was an early fan of the comics
and thought the X-Men would be

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:40.460
perfect for an animated series.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:44.180
So perfect in fact that Loesch
told her boss if "X-Men:

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:47.180
The Animated Series" doesn't
succeed, you can fire me.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:48.330
MARCELLUS: That's commitment.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:49.940
Putting it all on the line.

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:52.910
KENNETH: Once the series
got the green light in 1992,

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:55.070
Marvel and Fox agreed
to a core team.

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:57.620
Along with Wolverine,
Jubilee, and Storm,

00:01:57.620 --> 00:01:59.990
they added Cyclops,
Rogue, and Gambit.

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:03.490
Professor Xavier, Jean Grey,
and Beast rounded out the squad.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:04.290
Here we go.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.090
Who is this?

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:06.574
It is (SINGSONG) Magneto!

00:02:06.574 --> 00:02:08.539
MARCELLUS: Oh, I love Magneto.

00:02:08.539 --> 00:02:10.380
KENNETH: One of the best
villains of all time!

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:11.480
MARCELLUS: On the
count of three,

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:13.160
say your favorite
X-Men character.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:14.630
1, 2, 3--

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:15.800
BOTH: Storm!

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:16.910
MARCELLUS: Jinx.

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:19.490
According to creative
executive Sydney Iwanter,

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:21.710
it was important to focus
on these characters'

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:23.117
real emotional weaknesses.

00:02:23.117 --> 00:02:24.350
KENNETH: Well, here's
the thing, they

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:26.390
just wanted typical
super hero vulnerabilities.

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:28.468
We're talking about Rogue
not being able to touch

00:02:28.468 --> 00:02:29.435
anyone without consequences--

00:02:29.435 --> 00:02:30.330
MARCELLUS: Oh, absolutely.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.180
KENNETH: --Storm dealing
with being orphaned,

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:35.700
and even Wolverine dealing
with unrequited love.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:37.445
MARCELLUS: Oh, let's talk
about the love triangle--

00:02:37.445 --> 00:02:38.245
KENNETH: Oh, my.

00:02:38.245 --> 00:02:40.730
MARCELLUS: --that is Cyclops,
Wolverine, and Jean Grey.

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:42.890
And poor Wolverine, he was
supposed to be at the wedding.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:45.770
But he is mad because he is
in love with his frenemy's

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:46.970
wife, Jean Grey.

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:47.780
We all love Jean Grey.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:49.560
KENNETH: I feel like
Jean Grey was the glue.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:50.360
MARCELLUS: She was.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:51.380
KENNETH: She would always
come in and kind of just

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.150
make sure she was the
referee for everybody.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:55.100
 I can sense his feelings.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:56.197
They seem genuine.

00:02:56.197 --> 00:02:57.930
KENNETH: Just like Wolverine
that we see right here,

00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:59.390
I used to put forks
between my fingers.

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:00.350
MARCELLUS: Yes!
Yes!

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:01.460
I thought I was the only one.

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:02.780
I had my mamma's butter knife.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:03.580
KENNETH: Yes.

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:04.460
MARCELLUS: And I was
walking around the house

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:05.293
thinking I was Wolverine.

00:03:05.293 --> 00:03:06.800
"Boy, if you don't put
my butter knife back

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:07.610
in that drawer!"

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:08.990
KENNETH: I just
need pictures of you

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:11.705
in all your makeshift
X-Men costumes.

00:03:11.705 --> 00:03:13.820
And we can't forget
about my boy Morph.

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:16.170
He was only supposed
to be in one episode.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:18.500
But Fox had a focus group
with a couple hundred kids.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.900
And they voted for Morph
as their favorite mutant,

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.830
resurrected by popular demand.

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:25.130
MARCELLUS: The first season
had one continuous storyline.

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:27.140
But due to animation
delays, season

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:30.090
two's episodes were created
to stand on their own.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:31.910
So if one episode
wasn't finished on time,

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:33.530
another could be
shown in its place.

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:35.510
KENNETH: Networks at the
time didn't think kids could

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:37.280
follow complicated storylines.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.680
The series' writing
team disagreed, which

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:40.970
was definitely the right call.

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:43.430
And on behalf of kids
everywhere, we thank you.

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:44.790
MARCELLUS: Director
Larry Houston,

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:47.270
who was also the very
first Black Saturday

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:50.450
morning storyboard artist
to be hired in Hollywood,

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:54.080
was a big fan of legendary
comic book artist Jim Lee.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.790
Lee's X-Men
costume designs

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:58.790
varied between characters,
but shared similar colors

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:02.315
and overall style, and therefore
inspired the look for the show.

00:04:02.315 --> 00:04:03.800
KENNETH: We love to see it.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:06.680
And speaking of making some
changes in Hollywood, Houston

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:10.160
and showrunner Eric Lewald
had a whole new approach

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:11.400
to casting the series.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.490
The first batch of audition
tapes they received

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:14.810
were all too cartoonish.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:16.010
MARCELLUS: Voice
actors at the time

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:17.990
weren't used to playing
it straight, especially

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:19.459
for a Saturday morning cartoon.

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:21.950
So they ended up bringing in
serious theater actors from

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:23.570
Toronto to voice their X-Men.

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:24.695
KENNETH: And these
actors brought

00:04:24.695 --> 00:04:27.890
a gravitas and a grounding and
a realness to each character.

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:29.750
MARCELLUS: It was just
so amazing to hear it.

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:32.420
KENNETH: According to George
Buza, who voiced Beast,

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:35.300
the cast had to record all
of their dialogue lines first

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:38.090
because their voices would be
so worn out after doing battle

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:39.330
noises-- like this, Marcellus--

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:41.030
BOTH: [GRUNTING]

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:42.380
[LAUGHTER]

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:45.560
MARCELLUS: Still, all that
vocal strain paid off.

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:46.910
KENNETH: Before this
cartoon came out,

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:48.470
we didn't know how these
characters sounded.

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:49.270
MARCELLUS: We did not, we 
definitely did not.

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:50.580
KENNETH: They were
only on paper.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:53.330
So this is the first
time for us as fans

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:55.850
of the comic books to
actually hear the voice

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:57.050
of our favorite characters.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:04:58.490
MARCELLUS: And we loved it.

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:01.340
The series packed so much
story into 22 minutes,

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:03.800
way more than other
animated shows at the time.

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:07.640
KENNETH: With 40-page scripts
consisting of 400 to 500 shots,

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.070
it took more than
30,000 animated frames

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:12.290
to make a single episode--

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:14.570
totally unheard of
for a kids cartoon.

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:16.790
MARCELLUS: This was way
before computer animation.

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:19.640
So every single one of those
frames was painted by hand.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:21.410
KENNETH: Ooh, my hands are
cramping up just thinking

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:22.760
about all that painting.

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.890
MARCELLUS: And what
about the cameos

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:26.420
from the other Marvel heroes?

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:27.710
We got Captain
America right here,

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:29.510
who was already a big deal.

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:31.430
Hello, headline
news, we got X-Men.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:33.560
And then you turn around,
and we got new people?

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.870
Ken, I was just starstruck.

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:39.320
KENNETH: We have to shout out
Eric Lewald and Julia Lewald.

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:41.560
We found their book,
"X-Men: The Art and Making

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:43.580
of the Animated
Series," super helpful

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:44.990
when making this episode.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:47.030
If you're a fan of the
series, you'll love that book.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:48.090
Make sure you check it out.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:49.520
And that's our show for today.

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:50.800
MARCELLUS: Be sure
to like, subscribe,

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:52.870
and check out "X-Men:
The Animated Series,"

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:54.430
now streaming on Disney+.

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:56.440
KENNETH: Take care of
yourselves and the planet and.

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:57.490
We'll see you next time.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:59.170
Marcellus and Ken, signing off.

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:01.760
MARCELLUS: Storm would be both
of our favorite characters.

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:03.910
KENNETH: That's because we
spend too much time together.

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:04.870
MARCELLUS: You love it.

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:06.370
KENNETH: I do, I do.

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:09.420
[MUSIC PLAYING]

